Below is a short “data‑discovery road map” for answering the question, followed by ten illustrative BigQuery SQL statements that progress from simple inspection to the final correlation computation.  

Relevant columns and their use  
• 311 _service_requests  
  – `created_date` → convert to DATE to aggregate by day  
  – `complaint_type` → category whose proportions we will correlate  
• GSOD daily weather tables (`noaa_gsod.gsod20YY`)  
  – `stn`      → filter for ‘744860’ (JFK Airport)  
  – `wdsp`      → daily average wind‑speed (knots‑to‑tenths, cast to FLOAT64)  
  – `year`,`mo`,`da` → build calendar DATE for the join  

Global conditions that will be reused  
• 311 records with DATE(created_date) between ‘2011‑01‑01’ and ‘2020‑12‑31’  
• GSOD rows with `stn = '744860'` and `year` between ‘2011’ and ‘2020’  

--------------------------------------------------
10 BigQuery SQL queries
--------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Inspect the distribution of 311 rows by year (sample 20 rows)
-- Description: Quick check that the years 2011‑2020 really exist.
SELECT DISTINCT EXTRACT(YEAR FROM created_date) AS yr
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
ORDER BY yr
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Glimpse the different 311 complaint types
-- Description: A look at the dimension we will correlate.
SELECT DISTINCT complaint_type
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
ORDER BY complaint_type
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count total requests per complaint type (2011‑2020)
-- Description: We need this to keep only types with >3 000 requests.
SELECT
  complaint_type,
  COUNT(*) AS tot_reqs
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
GROUP BY complaint_type
ORDER BY tot_reqs DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same as #3 but show ONLY the qualifying types (tot_reqs > 3000)
-- Description: Creates the shortlist we will later correlate.
SELECT
  complaint_type,
  COUNT(*) AS tot_reqs
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
GROUP BY complaint_type
HAVING tot_reqs > 3000
ORDER BY tot_reqs DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Inspect one year of GSOD wind data for JFK (station 744860)
-- Description: sanity‑check wdsp values and date assembly for 2015.
SELECT
  PARSE_DATE('%Y-%m-%d', CONCAT(year,'-',mo,'-',da))          AS obs_date,
  CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64)                                       AS wind_knots
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod2015`
WHERE stn = '744860'
ORDER BY obs_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Build the 2011‑2020 daily wind‑speed series for JFK
-- Description: UNION ALL across the yearly GSOD tables with a wildcard.
SELECT
  PARSE_DATE('%Y-%m-%d', CONCAT(year,'-',mo,'-',da)) AS obs_date,
  CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64)                             AS wind_knots
FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod20*`
WHERE stn = '744860'
  AND year BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
  AND wdsp NOT IN ('999.9','9999.9')                -- remove “missing” codes
```

```sql
-- 7. Daily TOTAL of 311 requests city‑wide (2011‑2020)
-- Description: denominator for the daily proportions.
SELECT
  DATE(created_date)            AS req_date,
  COUNT(*)                      AS total_requests
FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
GROUP BY req_date
ORDER BY req_date
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Daily counts & proportions for ONE sample complaint type (‘Down Tree’)
-- Description: example of how the proportion time‑series is built.
WITH
daily_tot AS (
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, COUNT(*) AS tot
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
  GROUP BY d
),
daily_type AS (
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, COUNT(*) AS n_type
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
    AND complaint_type = 'Down Tree'
  GROUP BY d
)
SELECT
  t.d,
  n_type,
  tot,
  SAFE_DIVIDE(n_type,tot) AS prop_down_tree
FROM daily_tot AS t
LEFT JOIN daily_type USING(d)
ORDER BY d
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Compute Pearson correlation BETWEEN WIND and PROPORTION for ALL types
-- Description: produce correlation value per complaint type.
WITH
wind AS (                       -- 2011‑2020 JFK wind series
  SELECT
    PARSE_DATE('%Y-%m-%d', CONCAT(year,'-',mo,'-',da)) AS d,
    CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64) AS wdsp_knots
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod20*`
  WHERE stn = '744860'
    AND year BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
    AND wdsp NOT IN ('999.9','9999.9')
),
tot AS (                        -- daily total 311 requests
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, COUNT(*) AS tot
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
  GROUP BY d
),
by_type AS (                    -- daily counts per complaint type
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, complaint_type, COUNT(*) AS n
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
  GROUP BY d, complaint_type
),
props AS (                      -- join to build daily proportion
  SELECT
    b.complaint_type,
    b.d,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(b.n, t.tot) AS prop
  FROM by_type b
  JOIN tot t USING (d)
)
SELECT
  complaint_type,
  CORR(prop, wdsp_knots) AS corr_coeff
FROM props
JOIN wind USING (d)
GROUP BY complaint_type
HAVING COUNT(prop) > 30                -- keep types that appear often enough
       AND SUM(n) > 3000               -- same 3 000‑request filter
ORDER BY corr_coeff DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final answer: strongest POSITIVE and NEGATIVE correlations
-- Description: returns exactly two rows required by the task.
WITH
wind AS (
  SELECT
    PARSE_DATE('%Y-%m-%d', CONCAT(year,'-',mo,'-',da)) AS d,
    CAST(wdsp AS FLOAT64) AS wdsp_knots
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.noaa_gsod.gsod20*`
  WHERE stn = '744860'
    AND year BETWEEN '2011' AND '2020'
    AND wdsp NOT IN ('999.9','9999.9')
),
tot AS (
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, COUNT(*) AS tot
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
  GROUP BY d
),
by_type AS (
  SELECT DATE(created_date) AS d, complaint_type, COUNT(*) AS n
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.new_york.311_service_requests`
  WHERE DATE(created_date) BETWEEN '2011-01-01' AND '2020-12-31'
  GROUP BY d, complaint_type
),
props AS (
  SELECT
    b.complaint_type,
    b.d,
    SAFE_DIVIDE(b.n, t.tot) AS prop
  FROM by_type b
  JOIN tot t USING (d)
),
corrs AS (
  SELECT
    complaint_type,
    CORR(prop, wdsp_knots) AS corr_coeff,
    SUM(n)                 AS total_reqs
  FROM props
  JOIN wind USING (d)
  JOIN by_type USING (d, complaint_type)
  GROUP BY complaint_type
  HAVING total_reqs > 3000
)
SELECT *
FROM (
  (SELECT complaint_type, ROUND(corr_coeff,4) AS corr_coeff
   FROM corrs
   ORDER BY corr_coeff DESC
   LIMIT 1)
  UNION ALL
  (SELECT complaint_type, ROUND(corr_coeff,4) AS corr_coeff
   FROM corrs
   ORDER BY corr_coeff
   LIMIT 1)
);
```

Running the last query will return two rows – the complaint type whose daily share rises most when winds are strong (highest positive correlation) and the type whose share falls most (most negative correlation) – along with their Pearson coefficients rounded to four decimals.
