Below is a short “data‑discovery road map” for answering the question, followed by ten illustrative BigQuery SQL statements that progress from simple inspection to the final correlation computation.  

Relevant columns and their use  
• 311 _service_requests  
  – `created_date` → convert to DATE to aggregate by day  
  – `complaint_type` → category whose proportions we will correlate  
• GSOD daily weather tables (`noaa_gsod.gsod20YY`)  
  – `stn`      → filter for ‘744860’ (JFK Airport)  
  – `wdsp`      → daily average wind‑speed (knots‑to‑tenths, cast to FLOAT64)  
  – `year`,`mo`,`da` → build calendar DATE for the join  

Global conditions that will be reused  
• 311 records with DATE(created_date) between ‘2011‑01‑01’ and ‘2020‑12‑31’  
• GSOD rows with `stn = '744860'` and `year` between ‘2011’ and ‘2020’  

